"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KT1H7QB71S0NVJV\",\"title\":\"Climate smart rice farming in India — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"SUPERPOLLUTANTS\",\"Climate smart rice farming in India\",\"Mitti Labs\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"AB40\",\"Crediting period\",\"01 Jun 2025 to 01 Jun 2035\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"AB40\",\"approval\":\"Expected 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Rice Methane Reduction v1.0\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 1 of 1\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"07 Sep 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://mittilabs.earth\",\"t\":\"Mitti Labs\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/rice-methane-reduction/1.0\",\"t\":\"Rice Methane Reduction v1.0\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1KT1H5CM51S0EHVH\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KT1H5CM51S0EHVH/prj_1KT1H7QB71S0NVJV/pjd_1M1YAJW961S05PNQ/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nSUPERPOLLUTANTS\\nClimate smart rice farming in India\\nMitti Labs\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\nAB40\\nCrediting period\\n01 Jun 2025 to 01 Jun 2035\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nRice Methane Reduction v1.0\\nPublic comment period\\nThis project is in a public comment period from 07 Sep 2026 until 16 Sep 2026. Please send feedback to project-feedback@isometric.com.\\nSummary\\n\\nThe project, “Carbon Smart Rice Farming in India,” is implemented in accordance with the Isometric-certified protocol “Rice Methane Reduction, Version 1.0.” The project aims to reduce methane emissions from paddy cultivation across India by promoting the adoption of Alternate Wetting and Drying (AWD) irrigation practices. Under the baseline scenario, paddy fields are continuously flooded throughout the crop duration, creating anaerobic conditions that lead to significant methane emissions. In contrast, the project activity reduces the duration of field submergence by introducing controlled irrigation cycles, thereby limiting anaerobic decomposition and associated methane generation. Participating farmers are equipped with AWD field tubes, consisting of approximately 15 cm of perforated pipe installed below the soil surface and about 10 cm extending above ground. These tubes enable farmers to monitor subsurface water levels and make informed decisions on irrigation and drainage. During non-critical growth stages, fields are allowed to dry to a specified threshold before re-irrigation, as guided by the water levels observed in the tubes. Mitti Labs, in collaboration with local implementation partners, maintains a strong on-ground presence to support farmers through regular field visits, capacity building, and continuous data collection throughout the cropping seasons.\\n\\nSouthern India\\nHow carbon is being reduced\\n\\nSuperpollutant pathways target highly potent greenhouse gases, such as methane and refrigerants, whose near-term climate impact far exceeds that of carbon dioxide.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2026\\nAudit kick-off\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nSite visit\\n\\nIsometric’s qualified VVB conducts a site visit, comparing the project facility against the documentation provided. The required cadence for site visits is defined in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n07 Sep 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"